      "writtenOn": "2021-07-15T20:20:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The second CL results a configure error, complaining about \"defined without a type\". It is because, like Wealian said, the Zephyr kconfig.cmake does a ARCH-target sourcing. But our zephyr/app/ec/Kconfig does an unconditional sourcing. For example, in the asurada project, which is a non-ARM ARCH, the Zephyr upstream doesn\u0027t source the soc/arm/nuvoton_npcx/Kconfig, which defines the type, but the our zephyr/app/ec/Kconfig just defines the default value, without the type. A configure error happens.\n\nThe NPCX_HEADER_* are the first ones defined in the Zephyr soc/ directory. Other existing configs are not. So it hits this problem.\n\nA quick solution would be changing our zephyr/app/ec/Kconfig  to do a ARCH-target sourcing. So it aligns what the Zephyr upstream does.",
      "parentUuid": "a8a6f8da_2eeb5bd6",
      "revId": "fb99f29fd73f34c6609d78544195cdced700778b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
